{
  "$comment": [
    "THE keyboard shortcuts. One file, read by everything that shows them.",
    "",
    "There were three copies before this: an array in src/main.rs, another in",
    "src/sol/app.rs, and prose in docs/keys.md. They disagreed — `M` existed only",
    "on Solana, `m` only on EVM, and `s` was 'sell' in one list and 'sell a slice",
    "of the balance' in the other. Nobody was careless; three lists cannot be kept",
    "in step by remembering to.",
    "",
    "ONE KEY PER ENTRY. `[` and `]` are two rows, not one \"[  ]\" row. The grouped",
    "form read well and was useless as data: you could not look up what `]` does,",
    "and the collision check cannot see inside a string, so a future conflict on",
    "`]` would have shipped. It also hid `0` filed under \"slippage\" when the code",
    "has it clearing the price impact limit.",
    "",
    "control — [ and ] for buy size — shares a description and a row, but each key",
    "is still its own string. The first version of this file wrote those as \"[  ]\",",
    "which reads fine and is useless as data: you cannot look up what `]` does, and",
    "the collision test cannot see inside a string, so a future conflict on `]`",
    "would ship. That grouping also hid a real error, with `0` filed under",
    "\"slippage\" while the code has it clearing the price impact limit.",
    "",
    "FIELDS",
    "  key      what you press, one key per entry",
    "  desc     what they do, in as few words as say it",
    "  section  the group it belongs to, in the order sections first appear here",
    "  chains   which dashboards have it: evm, sol, or both",
    "",
    "A key on both chains is written ONCE. If it does different things on each,",
    "that is two entries and a sign the key is wrong.",
    "",
    "Adding a key here is what puts it in the in-app help, docs/keys.md and the",
    "website. A test fails if the docs fall behind."
  ],
